1
00:01:05,217 --> 00:01:11,217
A Charlie Brown Valentine is a family, animation,
romance film directed by Bill Melendez.

2
00:02:10,434 --> 00:02:16,434
Lovesick Charlie Brown hopes – still – to get a valentine from the Little Red-Haired Girl, as
does Sally from Linus, Lucy from Schroeder and Peppermint Patty from Charlie Brown.

3
00:03:15,652 --> 00:03:21,652
Charlie Brown (voice), played by Wesley Singerman.

4
00:04:20,869 --> 00:04:26,869
Lucy Van Pelt (voice), played by Lauren Schaffel.

5
00:05:26,086 --> 00:05:32,086
Linus Van Pelt (voice), played by Corey Padnos.

6
00:06:31,304 --> 00:06:37,304
Peppermint Patty (voice), played by Emily Lalande.

7
00:07:36,521 --> 00:07:42,521
Marcie (voice), played by Jessica D. Stone.

8
00:08:41,739 --> 00:08:47,739
Sally (voice), played by Nicolette Little.

9
00:09:46,956 --> 00:09:52,956
On September 10, 2025, Charlie Kirk, an American right-wing political activist, was assassinated at Utah Valley University in Orem, Utah, while
speaking at an outdoor campus debate planned by Turning Point USA, the conservative youth organization he co-founded and led.

10
00:10:52,173 --> 00:10:58,173
Kirk, aged 31, was a close ally of US president Donald Trump and a
highly influential figure in the MAGA movement.

11
00:11:57,391 --> 00:12:03,391
Shortly after the debate event began, with around 3,000 people in attendance, Kirk was fatally shot in the neck with a
single bullet by a gunman positioned on the roof of a building approximately 142 yards (130 m) away.

12
00:13:02,608 --> 00:13:08,608
Kirk was taken to a local hospital, where he was later pronounced dead.

13
00:14:07,826 --> 00:14:13,826
A manhunt for the shooter ended the following day when Tyler James Robinson, a
22-year-old from Washington, Utah, surrendered to the local sheriff.

14
00:15:13,043 --> 00:15:19,043
Prosecutors charged Robinson with aggravated murder on September 16 and announced they
would seek the death penalty, alleging a politically motivated attack.

15
00:16:18,260 --> 00:16:24,260
He has yet to enter a plea.

16
00:17:23,478 --> 00:17:29,478
The assassination was highlighted as an instance of increasing political violence
within the United States and was condemned by national and foreign leaders.

17
00:18:28,695 --> 00:18:34,695
Public reactions ranged from heartfelt messages expressing anguish
about the political climate to sharply partisan comments.

18
00:19:33,913 --> 00:19:39,913
Trump, members of the Republican Party, and other conservative figures blamed members of the Democratic Party
and left-wing or liberal beliefs before a suspect was in custody or a motive was identified.

19
00:20:39,130 --> 00:20:45,130
The Trump administration called for a crackdown against what it called "political extremism" on the left, which was widely criticized
by free speech advocates and legal experts as using the assassination as a pretext to silence political opposition.

20
00:21:44,347 --> 00:21:50,347
A campaign by right-wing organizations and US government agencies resulted in mass firings and disciplinary actions against
people seen as celebrating Kirk's death or making critical comments about him in the aftermath of the assassination.

21
00:22:49,565 --> 00:22:55,565
Kirk's memorial service was held at State Farm Stadium on September 21.

22
00:23:54,782 --> 00:24:00,782
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
